# Numbers on which the code of a multi-byte encoding (src/encoding/encoding_cjk.c) and the standard's text of it differ, for tools/encoding/check-transcription.py,
# each with where it is and the reason it is not a mistake. A number on one side only that is not here fails the check; so does an entry that no longer differs.
#
# region <TAB> number (decimal or 0x hex) <TAB> where <TAB> reason
#
# where: `note`  - the standard names it in a note or a name, not in a step;
#        `code`  - the code uses it and the standard's text does not name it (an implementation detail);
#        a path  - the standard's step names it and the code of the handlers does not, because the file named (relative to this library) holds it: the number must
#                  be used there.
